    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The joint and marginal probabilities, $ \\Pr(Q_k M_j) $ and $ \\Pr(M_j) $, are functions of the experimental design and the linkage map (the position of the putative QTLs with respect to the marker loci). Computing these probabilities is a relatively simple matter of bookkeeping (see Example 1), but can get rather tedious as the number of markers and/or QTLs under consideration increases.",
      "source_page": 447,
      "printed_page": 427,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter15:p003:b8"
      ],
