    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "We now move on to the conditional probabilities for other single-marker line cross designs, starting with backcrosses. For a $ B_{1} $ population, where the $ F_{1} $ is backcrossed to $ P_{1} $ (with genotype MMQQ), one parental gamete is always MQ. Hence, for a single-marker analysis, there are only two marker genotypes, MM and Mm. Using the frequencies for the four possible gametes (Example 1) of the $ F_{1} $ parent gives the following conditional probabilities",
