    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "For designs involving more than one generation of recombination, the single-generation recombination frequency c is simply replaced by a corrected frequency $ \\tilde{c} $ that is a function of the particular design. We consider three such designs: advanced intercross lines (AILs), recombinant inbred lines (RILs), and double-haploid lines (DHLs).",
      "source_page": 450,
      "printed_page": 430,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter15:p006:b2"
