    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the approximation holds for $ ct << 1 $ (Darvasi and Soller 1995, Liu et al. 1996). For example, if the marker-QTL recombination frequency is $ c = 0.01 $, only 1% of the $ F_2 $ gametes are recombinant ( $ M_q $, $ m_Q $), but this increases to 2.5% in an $ F_5 $ and 9.1% in an $ F_{20} $. The conditional genotype probabilities for an $ F_t $ AIL are given by the $ F_2 $-design expressions in Example 1, with $ \\tilde{c} $ substituted for $ c $.",
      "source_page": 450,
      "printed_page": 430,
      "source_block_ids": [
